:: Hopeless Cycle Ending A 6 [ending]
<<set _thermoDisable to true>>

당신의 연인이 당신을 이끌고 공터를 가로질러, 당신의 형제자매들에게로 간다. 제단 주위로 더 많은 작은 <span class="tentacle">구멍</span>들이 열리기 시작했다. 작고 가느다란 팔다리가 그 구멍을 통해 뻗어 나와, 구멍을 넓히려 애쓰고 있다.
<br><br>

<<worldFemale 'She' 'He'>> carves a cross into each and every one of their faces. <<worldFemale 'She' 'He'>> carves at least ten into the faces of the Bishop and the Hand.
<<worldFemale 'She' 'He'>> looks down at their entranced, helpless bodies smugly as <<worldFemale 'she' 'he'>> works.
<br><br>

<<worldFemale 'She' 'He'>> doesn't need to bend over or kneel to do it.
<<worldFemale 'Her' 'His'>> <span class="narration">monstrous</span> <span class="purple">beautiful</span> hands nearly touch the ground even when <<worldFemale 'she' 'he'>>'s standing.
<br><br>

당신의 연인은 그들을 보호하기 위한 것이라고 말한다.
<<if $prisonerBrands.includes("right cheek")>>
	You gently rub the cross branding on <<worldFemale 'her' 'his'>> face. <<worldFemale 'Her' 'His'>> head tilts into your touch as <<worldFemale 'she' 'he'>> smiles.
<</if>>
<<worldFemale 'Her' 'His'>> generosity and forgiveness are truly divine.
<br><br>

More tentacles emerge from <<worldFemale 'her' 'his'>> lower back, swirling around <<worldFemale 'her' 'his'>> waist in a blooming circle. Like a dress, or a flower.
<br><br>

당신의 연인이 당신을 숲속으로, 당신의 새로운 삶으로 이끈다.
<br><br>

<span class="narration">
	악마와 간수는 다시는 모습을 보이지 않았고, 수많은 수색대가 파견되었지만 그들을 찾지 못했다.
	<br><br>

	신도들은 무사했지만, 변해 있었다. 얼굴에 영원히 십자가가 새겨져, 그들의 실패를 영원히 상기시켰다.
	박해는 점차 잦아들었고, 그들의 광신적인 분노는 새로이 찾아온 겸손함에 억눌렸다.
	<br><br>

	The demon prized <<worldFemale 'her' 'his'>> pet above all else. A trophy, an insult to those who had tormented <<worldFemale 'her' 'him'>>.
	<<if $prisonerEvents.includes("love")>>
		Moreover, <<worldFemale 'her' 'his'>> cold heart began to feel affection for <<worldMale 'him' 'her'>> again.
		If there was a shred of humanity left in <<worldFemale 'her' 'him'>>, it was only because of the gaoler's warmth.
	<<else>>
		<<worldFemale 'She' 'He'>> defiled <<worldMale 'him' 'her'>> again and again, which kept <<worldFemale 'her' 'him'>> from turning into a true monster.
	<</if>>
	The two hid from the world, as <<worldFemale 'her' 'his'>> demonic appearance would become permanent.
	<br><br>

	The gaoler was happy. Being anything but happy was incomprehensible to <<worldMale 'him' 'her'>>, now.
	Was it all for this? Was <<worldMale 'he' 'she'>> merely a puppet? A tool? Did the demon ever hold true feelings for <<worldMale 'him' 'her'>>?
	Such thoughts never crossed <<worldMale 'his' 'her'>> mind. Even in <<worldMale 'his' 'her'>> rare instances of lucidity, <<worldMale 'he' 'she'>> merely appeared confused. <<worldMale 'He' 'She'>> made no attempt to escape.
	Perhaps even <<worldMale 'his' 'her'>> lucid mind was happy.
	<br><br>

	그리하여, <span class="green">사랑</span>의 절망의 굴레는 반복된다.
</span>
<<set $hc.ending to "A">>
<br><br>

